# Shape for an OpenTelemetry Collector service block appended under docker-compose.yml's
# `services:`. Speaks OTLP/HTTP on :4318 — the same port `management.otlp.tracing.endpoint`
# and `management.otlp.metrics.export.url` point at in application.yml. Vendor-neutral
# exporter (`debug`, dumps spans and metrics to its own stdout): no backend chosen yet —
# swap the exporter in `otel-collector-config.yml`, not this file, using the delta that
# ships inside `jaeger-service.yml.example` or `grafana-stack-service.yml.example`.
# Version resolved against the registry, not memory — same rule as every other version in
# this repo.
#
# **4318 is published, and the host port is variable.** The application has two ways to
# run, and each reaches the collector at a different address. Inside compose, the `app`
# service sets `OTLP_ENDPOINT`/`OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT` to `otel-collector:4318`. On the
# host (`./mvnw spring-boot:run`), the fragment's defaults point at `localhost:4318`, and
# only this mapping makes them answer. Without it, every export fails on the host (issue
# #66). It is the same host-first shape as postgres, mysql and kafka.
# Two sibling projects running at once compete for the host port. An orphan collector
# that answered this project's traffic with its own, older config is lessons-learned-008.
# `ArchHook.java compose` now reports the foreign holder and the service stuck in
# `Created`, and its gate blocks on both. Set OTLP_HTTP_PORT in one of the projects, and
# point that project's host-run OTLP_ENDPOINT and OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT at the same port.
  otel-collector:
    image: otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.160.0
    command: ["--config=/etc/otel-collector-config.yml"]
    ports:
      - "${OTLP_HTTP_PORT:-4318}:4318"
    volumes:
      - ./docker/init/otel-collector/otel-collector-config.yml:/etc/otel-collector-config.yml:ro
